I'm currently packing up Paul's collection. (The kids want the house back)

At this point the KL10, Drives & most documentation are going into a
container along with any non-media that will also fit (a '70, Multiple
VAXen, Several parts of some '8s etc).

In packing the collection I have only seen 3 DECtapes, I believe you may
have spoken to Tony Epton about this off-line.  I know where these are and
I'll pull them for you.

Once the gear goes into the container (next couple of weeks) it will be
difficult to find again.  If there is anything specific people are
interested in let me know asap (bruce-at-bicycle-dot-synonet-dot-com),
keeping in mind that we don't really want to split the '10 up - it'd be
nice to get it back into operation sometime in the future.

We can possibly get copies of media, although that'll be a longer term
project - all drives need cleaning & servicing & the media will probably
have to be extracted on a '750 or '70 as those are the only two machines I
could get up in a reasonable time with Massbus for the RP06 & RP07s.

Tapes were badly labeled & again need proper treatment before they're
extracted. There's about 3,000 tapes to be gone through in Paul's
collection so that would take some time.


As an aside, there are quite a few VAXen that will be looking for homes
(about 5 4000 series, multiple Micro-vax 2s) If anyone in Australia is
interested in giving this stuff a home and is willing to pay for shipping,
we can arrange that.


Bruce




